  "notes": "Continues the factorization through a common finite étale covering Y′. Equations (6)–(9) reduce isotopy of f and g to a self-homeomorphism u of X isotopic to the identity. Proposition 1 calls the maps “congrus” under the identity component of the automorphism group, with g=fu. This is precomposition, not conjugation, matching the visible word congrus. The proof’s substitution g=pg₀=p(f₀∘u)=(pf₀)u=f∘u checks directly. Conversely an isotopy u_t from the identity to u gives the family f∘u_t; this verifies the implication using the given isotopy setting.\n\nThe last sentence ends “peut-on le”; no continuation is supplied here. The displayed u is followed by a very short doubtful token, retained rather than silently removed. The correction applications -> morphismes includes a cancelled feminine e in finies. Bottom pencil number 3; no date or manuscript page number at the top.",
